			<div class="content" id="post-content-2877926">
									

<p>Thanks to everybody who reviewed this in chat! It's come a long way since its first iteration, and I'm reasonably happy with how it's turned out.</p>
<p>And yes, those are real Marx quotes embedded in the addendum. Isn't that something?</p>
<hr />
<hr />
<p><strong>Edit regarding communism, pseudo-communism, and variants thereof:</strong> Okay, so, it's been a little while since I posted this. I was unnecessarily defensive of myself when people criticised this (what with it being my first SCP and all), and I think it's time to explain myself properly.</p>
<p>This is not what I think communism is. I think communism is a pretty good ideology, to be honest (though it has problems like everything else), and this article is not me trying to slander either it, or the authors of the Communist Manifesto. I won't get into a discussion of communism's merits here (it's hardly the correct place), but you'll have to take my word for it.</p>
<p>This article is supposed to be a parody<sup>2</sup>, in a sense &#8212; it's me attempting to replicate the willful misinterpretation of communist ideals to suit an individual's own desires. A parody of the malicious parodies of communism, if you will. I completely failed to express that in a concise manner, and I only have myself to blame for that. Apologies to Flameshirt, TheShrike, q 17 and everyone else who I dragged into an unnecessary debate about what was intended as a harmless dig at misunderstanding: and no, the irony is not lost on me.</p>

